WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.334 --> 00:00:05.919
The world can be a toxic place.

00:00:07.671 --> 00:00:10.298
No one knows this more
than women and girls,

00:00:10.298 --> 00:00:12.092
cis and trans,

00:00:12.092 --> 00:00:13.677
as well as nonbinary people.

00:00:14.636 --> 00:00:16.346
I am a journalist

00:00:16.346 --> 00:00:17.681
with 30 years’ experience

00:00:17.681 --> 00:00:20.850
reporting on the injustices women
and others face around the world.

00:00:21.851 --> 00:00:25.063
I’m a co-founder of the Man Up Campaign

00:00:25.063 --> 00:00:29.234
to energize youth activism
against sexual and gender-based violence.

00:00:30.068 --> 00:00:32.404
I’m a father to two daughters,

00:00:32.404 --> 00:00:34.906
I’m a life partner to a woman

00:00:34.906 --> 00:00:36.408
and I’m a Black man in America.

00:00:37.826 --> 00:00:39.202
Holding these identities --

00:00:39.202 --> 00:00:41.913
and many more --

00:00:41.913 --> 00:00:44.624
I say this call to action to you

00:00:44.624 --> 00:00:45.917
with the deepest sincerity

00:00:45.917 --> 00:00:47.168
and utmost gravity.

00:00:48.878 --> 00:00:52.882
It is time for a gender reckoning,

00:00:52.882 --> 00:00:57.929
beginning with men authentically
confronting our internal selves

00:00:57.929 --> 00:00:59.264
and each other

00:00:59.264 --> 00:01:00.765
through the toxicity within us.

00:01:01.975 --> 00:01:05.854
Against the backdrop
of Black Lives Matter protest,

00:01:05.854 --> 00:01:09.816
cries for a racial reckoning
have echoed throughout the world,

00:01:09.816 --> 00:01:11.818
at times seeming premature

00:01:11.818 --> 00:01:13.069
and largely misunderstood.

00:01:14.404 --> 00:01:18.575
I believe a true gender reckoning
must be the center

00:01:18.575 --> 00:01:21.494
of any transformative movement
for social justice and equity.

00:01:22.746 --> 00:01:23.913
But what is a reckoning?

00:01:24.914 --> 00:01:28.335
Dictionaries say it means
to resolve a bill or a debt.

00:01:29.294 --> 00:01:31.338
In other words, to settle an account.

00:01:32.756 --> 00:01:34.674
In the case of women and girls,

00:01:34.674 --> 00:01:36.134
what is the debt owed to them?

00:01:36.968 --> 00:01:37.969
Who’s to pay it?

00:01:39.179 --> 00:01:40.180
And how?

00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:44.309
The consequences of male toxicity
continue building

00:01:44.309 --> 00:01:45.685
the debt to which I refer,

00:01:45.685 --> 00:01:47.228
including, among others,

00:01:47.228 --> 00:01:51.524
a gender wealth gap most affecting women
who care for their families

00:01:51.524 --> 00:01:54.152
as well as act as the primary
income generators

00:01:54.152 --> 00:01:55.153
for their households.

00:01:56.279 --> 00:02:00.408
Today, in the United States and abroad,

00:02:00.408 --> 00:02:06.665
threats to reproductive justice endanger
the lives and hard-fought rights of women

00:02:06.665 --> 00:02:11.586
in regards to their bodily,
sexual and gender autonomy,

00:02:11.586 --> 00:02:14.214
impacting the most disenfranchised
community in society.

00:02:15.298 --> 00:02:16.591
And violence against women,

00:02:16.591 --> 00:02:18.385
in all of its forms,

00:02:18.385 --> 00:02:20.720
still represents
an existential challenge,

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:23.431
as we’ve seen domestic violence
rise in the pandemic,

00:02:23.431 --> 00:02:25.642
as people were confined to their homes,

00:02:25.642 --> 00:02:28.645
we’ve seen online and public
harassment flourish,

00:02:28.645 --> 00:02:29.646
unabated.

00:02:30.313 --> 00:02:32.273
The sexual trafficking,

00:02:32.273 --> 00:02:33.358
prostitution,

00:02:33.358 --> 00:02:37.404
exploitation of women and girls
thrives as ever before.

00:02:39.114 --> 00:02:41.157
From where does this toxicity come

00:02:41.157 --> 00:02:42.158
and why?

00:02:42.325 --> 00:02:44.703
Men are not endangered,

00:02:44.703 --> 00:02:46.454
we’re not under assault,

00:02:46.454 --> 00:02:48.123
we’re not being unfairly maligned.

00:02:48.707 --> 00:02:52.836
In fact, it’s men, or certain types of
masculinity, that are the issue.

00:02:54.796 --> 00:02:56.798
To be clear,

00:02:56.798 --> 00:02:59.718
being a man does not make me

00:02:59.718 --> 00:03:01.553
or anyone else who identifies as a man

00:03:01.553 --> 00:03:02.595
inherently toxic.

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:05.432
But masculinity,

00:03:05.432 --> 00:03:07.183
in certain forms,

00:03:07.183 --> 00:03:08.893
can harm women,

00:03:08.893 --> 00:03:10.186
girls,

00:03:10.186 --> 00:03:11.688
nonbinary people

00:03:11.688 --> 00:03:12.981
and men

00:03:12.981 --> 00:03:14.816
through violence,

00:03:14.816 --> 00:03:16.151
dominating power

00:03:16.151 --> 00:03:17.152
and control.

00:03:17.944 --> 00:03:19.195
So how do we address this?

00:03:21.239 --> 00:03:24.033
How can we men step up

00:03:24.033 --> 00:03:26.161
and better support our daughters,

00:03:26.161 --> 00:03:27.829
our sisters,

00:03:27.829 --> 00:03:29.539
our female partners,

00:03:29.539 --> 00:03:31.624
our colleagues, neighbors and friends?

00:03:33.501 --> 00:03:38.089
Through what means can men both instigate
and lead a gender reckoning?

00:03:41.050 --> 00:03:43.762
First, we must tell the truth.

00:03:45.513 --> 00:03:47.599
We must tell the truth.

00:03:48.892 --> 00:03:52.687
Men grow into this world
becoming who we’re expected to be

00:03:52.687 --> 00:03:54.689
or who we think we’re expected to be

00:03:54.689 --> 00:03:56.816
based on cultural expectations

00:03:56.816 --> 00:03:58.651
and inaccurate historical narratives.

00:04:00.028 --> 00:04:03.865
As a short, chubby Black kid
wearing glasses growing up,

00:04:03.865 --> 00:04:06.910
I was repeatedly told I cried too much.

00:04:07.494 --> 00:04:08.995
I’m too emotional,

00:04:08.995 --> 00:04:09.996
too soft.

00:04:10.872 --> 00:04:14.459
It was ingrained in me
that to prove my masculinity

00:04:14.459 --> 00:04:16.377
I had to display physical prowess --

00:04:16.377 --> 00:04:17.378
intimidation.

00:04:18.171 --> 00:04:20.131
Because of that indoctrination,

00:04:20.131 --> 00:04:22.133
as an adult,

00:04:22.133 --> 00:04:25.929
I refused to seek help
facing escalating health challenges,

00:04:25.929 --> 00:04:27.806
including high blood pressure

00:04:27.806 --> 00:04:29.015
and mental trauma.

00:04:29.849 --> 00:04:32.811
The archetype of manhood nearly killed me.

00:04:34.646 --> 00:04:39.776
I say that as a survivor
of two heart attacks,

00:04:39.776 --> 00:04:41.653
four years on dialysis

00:04:41.653 --> 00:04:43.780
and a kidney transplant ...

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:46.157
aside from the physical risk
I put myself into

00:04:46.157 --> 00:04:47.659
covering wars around the world.

00:04:49.828 --> 00:04:52.622
The injury we do to ourselves

00:04:52.622 --> 00:04:54.707
and the women around us

00:04:54.707 --> 00:04:58.962
comes from fear of losing control,

00:04:58.962 --> 00:05:02.006
of lack of external affirmation

00:05:02.006 --> 00:05:03.299
and simply out of shame.

00:05:04.926 --> 00:05:06.761
Manhood is a spectrum of identities.

00:05:07.679 --> 00:05:09.264
There is no one way to be a man.

00:05:10.807 --> 00:05:14.352
And sometimes, discovering one’s true
manhood is a lifelong journey.

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:19.232
Secondly,

00:05:19.232 --> 00:05:20.483
we must be consistent.

00:05:22.026 --> 00:05:23.778
Men,

00:05:23.778 --> 00:05:26.239
especially men of color,

00:05:26.239 --> 00:05:30.410
cannot expect women to stand up for us,

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:34.080
with us in the face
of systemic oppressions

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:36.708
when too often we do not
do the same for them.

00:05:38.001 --> 00:05:39.002
(Applause and cheers)

00:05:39.002 --> 00:05:44.257
(Applause)

00:05:45.592 --> 00:05:48.303
The Black Lives Matter
movement for example,

00:05:48.303 --> 00:05:54.183
founded, named and led
by queer women of color,

00:05:54.183 --> 00:05:58.771
still centers Black men’s well-being

00:05:58.771 --> 00:06:01.190
in the face of unfair policing

00:06:01.190 --> 00:06:02.609
and criminal justice systems.

00:06:03.693 --> 00:06:06.362
And where’s the reciprocal
support from those men,

00:06:06.362 --> 00:06:08.197
including myself,

00:06:08.197 --> 00:06:12.660
in addressing intercommunity violence
against women of color,

00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:14.621
maternal health inequity,

00:06:14.621 --> 00:06:15.663
economic disparity?

00:06:16.623 --> 00:06:19.083
How and where do men show up for women?

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:23.338
I wonder ...

00:06:23.338 --> 00:06:27.634
how many men stood with women
on the steps of the US Supreme Court

00:06:27.634 --> 00:06:29.510
as they fought for reproductive rights?

00:06:30.595 --> 00:06:32.347
How many men should have been there?

00:06:33.306 --> 00:06:37.769
Finally, there can be no reckoning
without accountability.

00:06:39.437 --> 00:06:43.524
There can be no reckoning
without accountability.

00:06:45.526 --> 00:06:50.239
Men who commit acts of violence against
women must be held accountable

00:06:50.239 --> 00:06:52.909
by formal systems of justice

00:06:52.909 --> 00:06:54.160
as well as other men.

00:06:56.329 --> 00:07:00.875
Silence in the face of misogynistic
behavior and language is complicity.

00:07:01.668 --> 00:07:05.880
We men need to break free from the pack,

00:07:05.880 --> 00:07:09.634
take concrete actions to stop violence,

00:07:09.634 --> 00:07:10.843
create safety

00:07:10.843 --> 00:07:11.886
and build equity.

00:07:13.012 --> 00:07:14.889
And most importantly,

00:07:14.889 --> 00:07:16.099
say something.

00:07:17.225 --> 00:07:19.394
To be sure,

00:07:19.394 --> 00:07:24.273
bold men around us are actively working
to disrupt the narrative of male toxicity.

00:07:26.734 --> 00:07:29.237
After the 2010 earthquake in Haiti,

00:07:29.237 --> 00:07:30.655
a local organization,

00:07:30.655 --> 00:07:32.198
KOFAVIV,

00:07:32.198 --> 00:07:36.828
invited men to be defenders of women
and girls in displacement camps,

00:07:36.828 --> 00:07:39.247
women and girls who were
at risk of sexual assault.

00:07:40.456 --> 00:07:42.291
Scores of men answered the call

00:07:42.291 --> 00:07:44.085
and can continue to do so today.

00:07:44.919 --> 00:07:46.254
In New York City,

00:07:46.254 --> 00:07:47.880
CONNECT NYC,

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:49.757
led by a Black man,

00:07:49.757 --> 00:07:52.927
actively engages community partners
across civil society

00:07:52.927 --> 00:07:54.220
to address family violence.

00:07:55.054 --> 00:08:00.685
And in a profession not known generally
for its advocacy against gender violence,

00:08:00.685 --> 00:08:03.354
a professional player
for the Washington Football Team

00:08:03.354 --> 00:08:05.356
has become an unabashed advocate

00:08:05.356 --> 00:08:06.941
for men to learn

00:08:06.941 --> 00:08:10.945
and actively change behaviors
regarding sexual and physical violence.

00:08:12.488 --> 00:08:13.489
There is hope;

00:08:13.489 --> 00:08:14.490
there is light.

00:08:15.783 --> 00:08:17.994
Men around the world
are putting in the work

00:08:17.994 --> 00:08:20.288
to catalyze a true gender reckoning.

00:08:21.539 --> 00:08:22.707
But far more are needed.

00:08:23.916 --> 00:08:25.835
What I want to say to you today is this.

00:08:27.545 --> 00:08:28.546
Too many of us --

00:08:28.546 --> 00:08:30.173
too many men --

00:08:30.173 --> 00:08:32.133
don’t understand

00:08:32.133 --> 00:08:33.926
that equity,

00:08:33.926 --> 00:08:35.219
justice,

00:08:35.219 --> 00:08:36.763
inclusivity,

00:08:36.763 --> 00:08:41.350
safety for women, girls
and nonbinary people

00:08:41.350 --> 00:08:43.478
serves and saves us all.

00:08:44.687 --> 00:08:47.607
Broken masculinity harms societies,

00:08:47.607 --> 00:08:48.608
full stop.

00:08:49.233 --> 00:08:51.861
When we men reckon with that truth,

00:08:51.861 --> 00:08:53.863
we will finally find our shared humanity.

00:08:55.281 --> 00:08:56.491
Women,

00:08:56.491 --> 00:08:57.909
girls,

00:08:57.909 --> 00:08:59.660
nonbinary people,

00:08:59.660 --> 00:09:00.703
men

00:09:00.703 --> 00:09:03.247
standing together on equal footing

00:09:03.247 --> 00:09:04.499
with mutual respect

00:09:04.499 --> 00:09:06.334
in safe environments

00:09:06.334 --> 00:09:08.586
is the greatest
gender reckoning we can create.

00:09:09.295 --> 00:09:10.296
Thank you.

00:09:10.296 --> 00:09:11.422
(Applause and cheers)

